- Use an efficient in-memory structure for connected users to avoid costly lookups and broadcasts (msg 87, January-20-2024). The assistant recommended switching from arrays to a Map so inserts/deletes/lookup are O(1).

- Manage presence and rooms and avoid a global broadcast for every event (msg 101, January-20-2024). The assistant recommended authenticating sockets, tracking room membership, and only emitting to the room, which reduces unnecessary work under load.

- Debounce frequent UI events (typing indicators) to reduce event throughput (msg 313, February-18-2024). The assistant supplied a debounce example to reduce typing-event frequency:
const debounce = (func, wait) => {
let timeout;
return function(...args) {
clearTimeout(timeout);
timeout = setTimeout(() => func.apply(this, args), wait);
};
};
const emitTypingIndicator = debounce((socket, roomId) => {
socket.to(roomId).emit('typing', { userId: socket.userId });
